# Customer Credit Health Analysis

## Risk Distribution
**High-risk customers (8% of base) hold 58% of outstanding debt** — acute concentration risk. Low-risk segment (55% of customers) carries only 3% of outstanding, indicating strong segmentation.

| Tier | Count | Outstanding |
|------|-------|-------------|
| High | 29 | RM 6,587,822.96 |
| Moderate | 141 | RM 4,422,422.32 |
| Low | 205 | RM 339,617.24 |

## Top Offenders
**MY HERO HYPERMARKET SDN BHD** dominates: RM 2,112,369.4 outstanding (score 20, High Risk). Next two—MLF TRADING (RM 1,137,069) and LO SIEW LIN (RM 807,239.1)—both score ≤21, indicating severe payment discipline issues.

## Delinquency Pattern
Oldest accounts (PRIMA FRESH MART, LEONG HING: 1,850+ days overdue) carry modest balances (RM 3k–14k). These are **write-off candidates**, not material debt drivers. Conversely, major debtors (MY HERO, MLF) show recent delinquency, not historical aging.

## Credit Limit Breaches
Five customers exceed limits by 246–1,172%. **SEASONS AGRO** (1,172% utilization, RM 351,476 vs RM 30k limit) signals either inadequate limit-setting or material diversion of credit.

## Summary
High-risk segment is concentrated (29 customers = RM 6.6M), driven by operational delinquency, not aging invoices. Low-risk base (205 customers) is well-managed. Pattern suggests need for enhanced controls on top 10 customers.

